Plate NEW-2: on an empty Postgres the fourth migration already failed
(„UserAlias" does not exist): the twelve old Ally tables the code uses were
made by Ally's own tooling and no migration here ever created them; and the
unnumbered contact_insights.sql sorts after 016, which alters its table.
000_legacy_ally_base.sql creates those tables (generated from production's
catalogue, as they were before Netai's own migrations) and contact_insights
in the shape 016 leaves it — every statement guarded, so on production it
changes nothing. Checked on an empty Postgres 16: the server's own runner
applies all 238 migrations in one transaction; re-running the file on a
full database leaves the object count unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
